<title>PHILIPPINES: PNB cuts prime lending rate to 27 pct.</title>
<headline>PNB cuts prime lending rate to 27 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine National Bank said on Thursday it slashed its prime lending rate to 27 percent from 33 percent after the central bank's four percentage-point drop in the overnight borrowing rate to 28 percent.</p>
<p>Earlier, two other banks -- the Far East Bank and Trust Co and the Bank of the Philippine Islands -- cut their rates.</p>
<p>The central bank lowered its rate after the peso market showed some signs of normalisation.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8937</p>
</text>
